;; Book of Your Own Dialect — Appendix C — Real-Analog Table

(chapter
  :audience             programmer-learning-motoi
  :dialect              motoi
  :voice                motoi-copilot
  :training-eligible    #t
  :confidentiality      public
  :book             "Book of Your Own Dialect"
  :chapter-number   0
  :appendix         "C"
  :title            "Appendix C — Real-Analog Table"
  :prose
"# Appendix C — Real-Analog Table

Appendix A cataloged the strays and named their reasons. This appendix is the *conversion table*: for each common other-dialect verb, the real Motoi verb that does the same job, with a runnable proof of the Motoi side. The other-dialect names stay in prose and inline code — generic, so they stand for whole families of dialects rather than any one product. The runnable fences are always the Motoi analog, so this appendix is a workbench you can lift code off of directly.

Where a stray has no analog, the honest entry says so; but most everyday operations *do* cross over cleanly, because the ideas — map, filter, accumulate, look up, build a string — are universal even when the spellings aren't.

## Loading and modules

The loading family all maps to the same Motoi analog: nothing. The library is already present.

- other-dialect `require` / `use-modules` / `import` / `use` → Motoi: **nothing to write; libraries auto-load.**

The proof is that a verb from a library you never announced simply works. No line preceded this; the SRFI-13 verb was already here:

```scheme
;; The 'require' analog is the absence of require. This just runs.
(string-join (list \"already\" \"loaded\") \" \")
```

## Mapping a function over a list

- other-dialect `mapcar` / `arr.map(f)` / `map(f, xs)` / `sapply(xs, f)` / `xs.map(f)` → Motoi: **`map`**

```scheme
;; mapcar / .map / map(...) -> Motoi map.
(map (lambda (x) (* x x)) (list 1 2 3 4 5))
```

## Mapping for side effects (iteration)

- other-dialect `mapc` / `.forEach(f)` / `for x in xs: f(x)` / `.each { |x| ... }` → Motoi: **`for-each`**

```scheme
;; mapc / .forEach / for-loop for side effects -> for-each.
(let ((total 0))
  (for-each (lambda (x) (set! total (+ total x))) (list 1 2 3 4))
  total)
```

## Mapping and flattening (flat-map / concatMap)

- other-dialect `mapcan` / `flatMap` / `concatMap` / `xs.flatMap(f)` → Motoi: **`append-map`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; mapcan / flatMap / concatMap -> SRFI-1 append-map.
(append-map (lambda (x) (list x (* x x))) (list 1 2 3))
```

## Filtering / selecting elements

- other-dialect `remove-if-not` / `arr.filter(p)` / `select` / `filter(p, xs)` / `xs.select { |x| ... }` → Motoi: **`filter`**

```scheme
;; select / .filter / remove-if-not -> Motoi filter.
(filter even? (list 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8))
```

## Removing elements that match

- other-dialect `remove-if` / `reject` / `xs.reject { |x| ... }` → Motoi: **`remove`**

```scheme
;; remove-if / reject -> Motoi remove (keeps the ones that DON'T match).
(remove even? (list 1 2 3 4 5 6))
```

## Accumulating (left fold)

- other-dialect `fold-left` (acc-first) / `foldl` / `reduce(f, init, xs)` / `xs.foldLeft(init)(f)` / `xs.inject(init) { |acc, x| ... }` → Motoi: **`fold`** (element-first: procedure gets `(elem acc)`)

```scheme
;; fold-left / foldl -> Motoi SRFI-1 fold. Note element-first order.
(fold + 0 (list 10 20 30 40))
```

The order flip is real, so when the operation cares which argument is which, the Motoi call reads `(elem acc)`. Building a list with `cons` shows it: element first means prepend, so the fold reverses.

```scheme
;; Element-first fold: (fold cons '() ...) reverses.
(fold cons '() (list 1 2 3 4))
```

## Accumulating (right fold)

- other-dialect `foldr` / `fold-right` (acc-first) / `xs.foldRight(init)(f)` → Motoi: **`fold-right`** (SRFI-1, element-first)

```scheme
;; foldr -> Motoi fold-right (SRFI-1). Preserves order when consing.
(fold-right cons '() (list 1 2 3 4))
```

## Simple reduce with an operator

- other-dialect `reduce` / `inject` / `sum` / `xs.reduce(f)` → Motoi: **`reduce`** (SRFI-1) or **`fold`**

```scheme
;; reduce / inject / sum -> Motoi reduce (or fold with the same operator).
(list (reduce + 0 (list 3 6 9))
      (reduce max 0 (list 4 9 2 7)))
```

## List comprehension

- other-dialect `[f(x) for x in xs if p(x)]` / `for/list` / `(list comprehension)` → Motoi: **`map` over `filter`**

```scheme
;; [x*x for x in xs if even x] -> map over filter. Mine.
(map (lambda (x) (* x x))
     (filter even? (list 1 2 3 4 5 6)))
```

## Pipeline / threading

- other-dialect `->>` / `|>` / `.stream().map().filter()` / `xs.map(f).filter(p)` → Motoi: **nested calls**

```scheme
;; A pipeline (inc every element, keep evens) -> nested filter/map. Mine.
(filter even? (map (lambda (x) (+ x 1)) (list 1 2 3 4 5)))
```

## Building a range

- other-dialect `range(n)` / `range(a, b)` / `(0..n)` / `upto` / `1..=n` (Rust) → Motoi: **`iota`**

```scheme
;; range(5) -> iota 5; range with start -> (iota count start).
(list (iota 5)
      (iota 5 10)
      (iota 5 0 2))
```

## Pairing elements from two lists (zip)

- other-dialect `zip(xs, ys)` / `zipWith(f, xs, ys)` / `xs.zip(ys)` / `Enum.zip(xs, ys)` → Motoi: **`map` with two lists** (or `map list` for pairing)

```scheme
;; zip(xs, ys) -> (map list xs ys); zipWith f xs ys -> (map f xs ys).
(list (map list (list 1 2 3) (list \"a\" \"b\" \"c\"))
      (map + (list 1 2 3) (list 10 20 30)))
```

## Index access

- other-dialect `xs[i]` / `nth` / `elt` / `xs.get(i)` → Motoi: **`list-ref`** (lists) or **`vector-ref`** (vectors)

```scheme
;; xs[2] -> list-ref; vector index -> vector-ref.
(list (list-ref (list 10 20 30 40) 2)
      (vector-ref (vector 10 20 30 40) 1))
```

## Key lookup in an association list

- other-dialect `assoc-get` / alist helpers / `dict[k]` on a small map → Motoi: **`assoc`** (returns the pair)

```scheme
;; dict[k] on an alist -> assoc (returns the (key . value) pair, or #f).
(let ((prices (list (list \"pen\" 2) (list \"pad\" 5) (list \"ink\" 8))))
  (list (assoc \"pad\" prices)
        (assoc \"nope\" prices)))
```

## Key lookup in a hash map

- other-dialect `dict.get(k, default)` / `gethash` / `hashtable-ref` / `m[k]` → Motoi: **`hash-table-ref/default`** (SRFI-125)

```scheme
;; dict.get(k, default) / gethash -> hash-table-ref/default (SRFI-125).
(define d (hash-table))
(hash-table-set! d \"x\" 42)
(list (hash-table-ref/default d \"x\" 0)
      (hash-table-ref/default d \"y\" -1))
```

## Checking if a key exists in a hash map

- other-dialect `k in dict` / `dict.containsKey(k)` / `m.has(k)` → Motoi: **`hash-table-contains?`** (SRFI-125)

```scheme
;; 'k in dict' / containsKey / has -> hash-table-contains?.
(define h (hash-table))
(hash-table-set! h \"present\" 1)
(list (hash-table-contains? h \"present\")
      (hash-table-contains? h \"absent\"))
```

## Removing a key from a hash map

- other-dialect `del dict[k]` / `dict.remove(k)` / `m.delete(k)` → Motoi: **`hash-table-delete!`** (SRFI-125)

```scheme
;; del dict[k] / remove -> hash-table-delete!.
(let ((h (hash-table)))
  (hash-table-set! h \"k\" 99)
  (hash-table-delete! h \"k\")
  (hash-table-size h))
```

## Enumerating hash-table entries

- other-dialect `dict.items()` / `dict.entries()` / `m.entrySet()` → Motoi: **`hash-table->alist`** or **`hash-table-keys` + `hash-table-values`**

```scheme
;; dict.items() -> hash-table->alist (returns list of (key . value) pairs).
(let ((h (hash-table)))
  (hash-table-set! h \"a\" 1)
  (hash-table-set! h \"b\" 2)
  (hash-table->alist h))
```

## Counting with a map / tally

- other-dialect `Counter` / `frequencies` / `group-by count` / `tally` → Motoi: **hash table + `hash-table-update!/default`**

```scheme
;; Counter / frequencies -> hash-table-update!/default idiom.
(define freq (hash-table))
(for-each
  (lambda (c) (hash-table-update!/default freq c (lambda (n) (+ n 1)) 0))
  (list \"a\" \"b\" \"a\" \"c\" \"a\" \"b\"))
(list (hash-table-ref/default freq \"a\" 0)
      (hash-table-ref/default freq \"b\" 0)
      (hash-table-ref/default freq \"c\" 0))
```

## String: uppercase / lowercase

- other-dialect `s.upcase` / `toUpperCase` / `str.upper()` → Motoi: **`string-upcase`** / **`string-downcase`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; .upcase / toUpperCase -> string-upcase (SRFI-13).
(list (string-upcase \"motoi\")
      (string-downcase \"SCHEME\"))
```

## String: join a list of strings

- other-dialect `xs.join(sep)` / `String.join(sep, xs)` / `strings.Join(xs, sep)` → Motoi: **`string-join`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; xs.join(\"-\") -> string-join.
(string-join (list \"a\" \"b\" \"c\") \"-\")
```

## String: split on a separator

- other-dialect `s.split(sep)` / `str.split(sep)` / `strings.Split(s, sep)` → Motoi: **`string-split`**

```scheme
;; s.split(\"-\") -> string-split.
(string-split \"a-b-c-d\" \"-\")
```

## String: contains / index-of

- other-dialect `s.includes(t)` / `indexOf` / `contains?` / `in` / `str.find(t)` → Motoi: **`string-contains`** (returns index or #f)

```scheme
;; s.includes(t) / indexOf -> string-contains (index, or #f if absent).
(list (string-contains \"motoi scheme\" \"scheme\")
      (string-contains \"motoi scheme\" \"zzz\"))
```

## String: prefix / suffix test

- other-dialect `startsWith` / `endsWith` / `str.startswith(p)` / `HasPrefix` → Motoi: **`string-prefix?`** / **`string-suffix?`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; startsWith / endsWith -> string-prefix? / string-suffix?.
(list (string-prefix? \"mo\" \"motoi\")
      (string-suffix? \"oi\" \"motoi\"))
```

## String: strip whitespace

- other-dialect `str.strip()` / `str.trim()` / `lstrip` / `rstrip` / `String.TrimSpace` → Motoi: **`string-trim`** / **`string-trim-right`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; strip / trim -> string-trim (left) and string-trim-right (right).
(list (string-trim \"   hello\")
      (string-trim-right \"hello   \"))
```

## String: reverse

- other-dialect `s[::-1]` / `s.reverse` / `String.reverse(s)` → Motoi: **`string-reverse`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; s.reverse / s[::-1] -> string-reverse. SRFI-13.
(string-reverse \"motoi\")
```

## String: pad to width

- other-dialect `str.ljust(n)` / `str.rjust(n)` / `PadLeft` / `PadRight` → Motoi: **`string-pad-right`** / **`string-pad`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; ljust / PadRight -> string-pad-right; rjust / PadLeft -> string-pad.
(list (string-pad-right \"hi\" 8)
      (string-pad \"hi\" 8))
```

## String: number to text and back

- other-dialect `str(n)` / `parseInt(s)` / `to_s` / `atoi` / `itoa` → Motoi: **`number->string`** / **`string->number`**

```scheme
;; str(n) / parseInt(s) -> number->string / string->number.
(list (number->string 255)
      (string->number \"42\"))
```

## String: extract a substring

- other-dialect `s[a:b]` / `s.substring(a, b)` / `substr(s, a, b)` → Motoi: **`substring`** (R7RS-small) or **`string-take` / `string-drop`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; s[1:4] / substring -> Motoi substring or string-take/drop.
(list (substring \"motoi-scheme\" 1 5)
      (string-take (string-drop \"motoi-scheme\" 6) 6))
```

## Sorting

- other-dialect `sort(xs)` / `sorted(xs)` / `xs.sort()` / `xs.sortBy(f)` → Motoi: **`sort`** with an explicit comparator

```scheme
;; sorted(xs) -> sort with a comparator; ascending and descending.
(list (sort (list 3 1 4 1 5) <)
      (sort (list 3 1 4 1 5) >))
```

Sorting by a key function (sort-by a property):

```scheme
;; sort-by-length: sort strings by their length. sort with a key comparator.
(sort (list \"gamma\" \"a\" \"do\" \"beta\")
      (lambda (a b) (< (string-length a) (string-length b))))
```

## Deduplicate

- other-dialect `set(xs)` / `uniq` / `distinct` / `nub` / `uniqBy` → Motoi: **`delete-duplicates`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; set(xs) / uniq / distinct -> delete-duplicates.
(delete-duplicates (list 1 1 2 3 3 3 4 4 5))
```

## Take / drop / slice

- other-dialect `take(n)` / `head` / `xs[:n]` and `drop(n)` / `tail` / `xs[n:]` → Motoi: **`take`** / **`drop`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; xs[:2] and xs[2:] -> take / drop.
(let ((xs (list 10 20 30 40 50)))
  (list (take xs 2)
        (drop xs 2)))
```

## Take-while / drop-while

- other-dialect `takeWhile(p, xs)` / `xs.takeWhile(p)` / `itertools.takewhile` → Motoi: **`take-while`** / **`drop-while`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; takeWhile / dropWhile -> SRFI-1 take-while / drop-while.
(list (take-while even? (list 2 4 6 7 8))
      (drop-while even? (list 2 4 6 7 8)))
```

## Find first match / any / all

- other-dialect `find` / `some` / `every` / `all` / `detect` / `any?` / `all?` → Motoi: **`find`** / **`any`** / **`every`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; find/some/all -> find / any / every.
(let ((xs (list 1 3 4 5 7)))
  (list (find even? xs)
        (any even? xs)
        (every odd? xs)))
```

## Count matching elements

- other-dialect `count(p, xs)` / `xs.count { |x| p(x) }` / `len(filter(p, xs))` → Motoi: **`count`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; count matching elements -> SRFI-1 count.
(count odd? (list 1 2 3 4 5 6))
```

## Split into matches and non-matches

- other-dialect `partition(p, xs)` / `xs.partition { |x| p(x) }` / `Seq.partition` → Motoi: **`partition`** (SRFI-1, two values)

```scheme
;; partition -> SRFI-1 partition. Two values: call-with-values to capture.
(call-with-values
  (lambda () (partition even? (list 1 2 3 4 5 6)))
  list)
```

## Build a list by index / list-tabulate

- other-dialect `Array.from({length: n}, (_, i) => f(i))` / `tabulate` / `generate` → Motoi: **`list-tabulate`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; Array.from or tabulate by index -> list-tabulate. SRFI-1.
(list-tabulate 6 (lambda (i) (* i i)))
```

## Counting the loop / iterating with an index

- other-dialect `for (i = 0; i < n; i++)` / `for i in range(n)` → Motoi: **named `let` recursion** (or `iota` + `for-each`)

```scheme
;; C-style counting for-loop -> named-let recursion.
(let loop ((i 0) (acc 0))
  (if (>= i 5) acc (loop (+ i 1) (+ acc i))))
```

Or using `iota` and `for-each` for indexed side-effecting iteration:

```scheme
;; Indexed iteration: iota generates indices, for-each walks them.
(let ((result (hash-table)))
  (for-each (lambda (i)
              (hash-table-set! result i (* i i)))
            (iota 5))
  (hash-table-ref/default result 3 0))
```

## Multiple values from a single call

- other-dialect tuple return / `(a, b) := f()` / `var a, b = f()` → Motoi: **multiple values** with **`call-with-values`** or **`let-values`**

```scheme
;; Multiple return values: call-with-values or let-values.
(let-values (((a b) (values 10 20)))
  (list a b (+ a b)))
```

## Exponentiation

- other-dialect `x**n` / `pow(x, n)` / `Math.pow(x, n)` / `x^n` → Motoi: **`expt`** (R7RS-small)

```scheme
;; x**n / pow(x,n) -> expt. R7RS-small core, mine.
(list (expt 2 10)
      (expt 3 4))
```

## Quotient and remainder

- other-dialect `div` / `mod` (R6RS exact integer division) / `%` → Motoi: **`quotient`** and **`remainder`** (R7RS-small)

```scheme
;; div / mod -> quotient and remainder. R7RS-small.
(list (quotient 17 5)
      (remainder 17 5)
      (modulo 17 5))
```

## Maximum and minimum of a list

- other-dialect `max(xs)` / `min(xs)` / `xs.max` / `xs.min` → Motoi: **`apply max xs`** or **`reduce max 0 xs`**

```scheme
;; max(xs) / xs.max -> (apply max xs) or (reduce max first-elem xs).
(let ((xs (list 3 7 1 9 4)))
  (list (apply max xs)
        (apply min xs)
        (reduce max 0 xs)))
```

## Random integer / random real

- other-dialect `random.randint(0, n)` / `Math.random()` / `rand()` → Motoi: **`random-integer`** / **`random-real`** (SRFI-27)

```scheme
;; random.randint / Math.random -> random-integer / random-real. SRFI-27.
(list (random-integer 100)
      (random-real))
```

## Symbol / keyword to string and back

- other-dialect `name.to_s` / `symbol_to_string` / `str(sym)` → Motoi: **`symbol->string`** / **`string->symbol`** (R7RS-small)

```scheme
;; symbol->string and string->symbol. R7RS-small core.
(list (symbol->string 'hello)
      (string->symbol \"world\"))
```

## Current time

- other-dialect `time.time()` / `Date.now()` / `System.currentTimeMillis()` / `now()` → Motoi: **`time/now`** (milliseconds since epoch)

```scheme
;; time.time() / Date.now() -> time/now. Motoi library, auto-loaded.
(let ((ms (time/now)))
  (> ms 0))
```

## Store a fact in long-term memory

- other-dialect (no standard analog) → Motoi: **`cortex/remember`** (or `cortex/write` for default salience)

```scheme
;; Long-term memory store: cortex/remember with a key and value.
(cortex/remember \"dialect/name\" \"Motoi Scheme, R7RS-small + SRFIs\")
(cortex/recall   \"dialect/name\")
```

## Building a list of repeated values (make-list)

- other-dialect `replicate n x` (Haskell) / `[x] * n` (Python) / `Collections.nCopies(n, x)` (Java) → Motoi: **`make-list`** (R7RS-small) or **`list-tabulate`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; replicate / nCopies -> make-list or list-tabulate.
(list (make-list 5 0)
      (list-tabulate 5 (lambda (i) (* i 2))))
```

## Take-while / drop-while as span

- other-dialect `span(p, xs)` (Haskell/SRFI-1 name) / `itertools.takewhile` paired with rest → Motoi: **`take-while`** and **`drop-while`** together (SRFI-1; `span` itself may not be wired — use the confirmed pair)

```scheme
;; span: both halves via take-while and drop-while. SRFI-1.
(let ((xs (list 2 4 6 7 8 10)))
  (list (take-while even? xs)
        (drop-while even? xs)))
```

## Flat-map / concatMap / collect

- other-dialect `flatMap` / `concatMap` / `List.collect f xs` (F#) / `Enum.flat_map` (Elixir) / `xs.flatMap(f)` (Swift/Kotlin) → Motoi: **`append-map`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; All the flat-map names -> SRFI-1 append-map.
(append-map (lambda (x) (list x (- x) (* x x)))
            (list 1 2 3))
```

## Compact-map / filter-map

- other-dialect `compactMap` (Swift) / `filterMap` (various) / `catMaybes` (Haskell) → Motoi: **`filter-map`** (SRFI-1; applies function, discards `#f` results)

```scheme
;; compactMap / catMaybes -> SRFI-1 filter-map.
(filter-map (lambda (x) (and (even? x) (* x x)))
            (list 1 2 3 4 5 6))
```

## Unfold (generating a list from a seed)

- other-dialect `unfoldr` (Haskell) / `iterate-while` / `Stream.iterate(...).takeWhile(...)` (Java) → Motoi: **`unfold`** (SRFI-1: stop-predicate, mapper, stepper, seed)

```scheme
;; unfoldr / iterate-while -> SRFI-1 unfold. Powers of 2 up to 64.
(unfold (lambda (n) (> n 64))
        (lambda (n) n)
        (lambda (n) (* n 2))
        1)
```

## Concatenate a list of lists

- other-dialect `concat` (Haskell/Clojure) / `flatten(1)` (one-level) / `chain.from_iterable` (Python) → Motoi: **`concatenate`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; concat / chain.from_iterable -> SRFI-1 concatenate.
(concatenate (list (list 1 2) (list 3 4 5) (list 6)))
```

## Fresh list copy

- other-dialect `xs[:]` (Python) / `List.copyOf(xs)` (Java) / `xs.clone()` → Motoi: **`list-copy`** (SRFI-1)

```scheme
;; Python xs[:] / Java List.copyOf -> SRFI-1 list-copy. Fresh spine.
(let* ((original (list 10 20 30))
       (copy     (list-copy original)))
  (equal? original copy))
```

## Group-by (build a map from a key function)

- other-dialect `groupBy(key)` (Kotlin/Scala) / `Enum.group_by(xs, key)` (Elixir) / `itertools.groupby` (Python) / `List.groupBy` (F#) → Motoi: **fold into a hash table**

```scheme
;; groupBy key -> fold + hash-table-update!/default accumulating lists.
(define (group-by xs key)
  (fold (lambda (x tbl)
          (hash-table-update!/default tbl (key x) (lambda (lst) (cons x lst)) '())
          tbl)
        (hash-table)
        xs))
(hash-table-ref/default (group-by (list 1 2 3 4 5 6) even?) #t '())
```

## Numeric: floor division and integer truncation

- other-dialect `//` (Python integer division) / `Math.floor(a/b)` (JS) / `div` (various) → Motoi: **`quotient`** (truncates toward zero) or **`floor`** applied to a division

```scheme
;; Python // -> quotient for integer division; floor for floor division of reals.
(list (quotient 17 5)
      (floor (/ 17.0 5.0)))
```

## Vector operations

- other-dialect `[x*x for x in v]` vector map / `v.map(f)` / `Array.map` → Motoi: **`vector->list`**, then **`map`**, then **`list->vector`** (or just work with the list)

```scheme
;; vector map: convert, map, convert back. R7RS-small path.
(list->vector
  (map (lambda (x) (* x x))
       (vector->list (vector 1 2 3 4 5))))
```

Vector fill and copy are R7RS-small core:

```scheme
;; vector-fill! and vector-copy: both R7RS-small.
(let ((v (make-vector 4 0)))
  (vector-fill! v 7 1 3)
  (list (vector->list v)
        (vector->list (vector-copy v 1 3))))
```

## Character: case and classification

- other-dialect `c.isalpha()` / `char.IsLetter(c)` / `Character.isLetter(c)` → Motoi: **`char-alphabetic?`** (R7RS-small)
- other-dialect `c.lower()` / `char.ToLower(c)` → Motoi: **`char-downcase`** (R7RS-small)
- other-dialect `c.upper()` / `char.ToUpper(c)` → Motoi: **`char-upcase`** (R7RS-small)
- other-dialect `ord(c)` (Python) / `(int) c` (C/Java) → Motoi: **`char->integer`** (R7RS-small)
- other-dialect `chr(n)` (Python) / `(char) n` (C/Java) → Motoi: **`integer->char`** (R7RS-small)

```scheme
;; Character classification and conversion: all R7RS-small.
(list (char-alphabetic? #\\m)
      (char-numeric? #\\5)
      (char-downcase #\\Z)
      (char-upcase #\\a)
      (char->integer #\\A)
      (integer->char 122))
```

## String: count characters matching a predicate

- other-dialect `sum(1 for c in s if p(c))` (Python) / `s.count(ch)` (Python) / `xs.Count(p)` (C#) → Motoi: **`string-count`** (SRFI-13)

```scheme
;; Python sum(1 for c ...) / .count() -> SRFI-13 string-count.
(list (string-count \"hello world\" char-alphabetic?)
      (string-count \"abc123xyz\" char-numeric?))
```

## String: case-insensitive comparison

- other-dialect `str.equalsIgnoreCase(t)` (Java) / `s.lower() == t.lower()` (Python) / `strcasecmp` (C) → Motoi: **`string-ci=?`** (R7RS-small) or **`string-ci<?`** etc.

```scheme
;; Case-insensitive string comparison: R7RS-small string-ci=? and friends.
(list (string-ci=? \"Hello\" \"hello\")
      (string-ci<? \"abc\" \"ABD\"))
```

## String: substring extraction (copy)

- other-dialect `s[start:end]` (Python) / `s.substring(a, b)` (Java) / `substr(s, a, len)` (C) → Motoi: **`substring`** (R7RS-small, start and end indices) or **`string-copy`** with bounds

```scheme
;; s[1:4] -> substring (R7RS-small) or string-copy with bounds.
(list (substring \"motoi-scheme\" 1 5)
      (string-copy \"motoi-scheme\" 6 12))
```

## Membership test in a list

- other-dialect `x in xs` (Python) / `xs.contains(x)` (Kotlin/Swift) / `xs.indexOf(x) >= 0` (JS) → Motoi: **`member`** (R7RS-small, `equal?` equality) or **`memv`** (`eqv?`) or **`memq`** (`eq?`)

```scheme
;; Python 'x in xs' / .contains(x) -> member. Returns the tail starting at x, or #f.
(list (member 3 (list 1 2 3 4 5))
      (member 9 (list 1 2 3 4 5)))
```

## String: per-character side effects

- other-dialect `for c in s: f(c)` (Python) / `s.forEach(f)` (JS on chars) / `for (char c : s.toCharArray())` (Java) → Motoi: **`string-for-each`** (R7RS-small)

```scheme
;; Per-character iteration for side effects: R7RS-small string-for-each.
(let ((count 0))
  (string-for-each
    (lambda (c) (when (char-alphabetic? c) (set! count (+ count 1))))
    \"hello world 42\")
  count)
```

## Parallel iteration (for-each over two lists)

- other-dialect `zip(xs, ys)` used in a `for` loop / `zip(*iters)` (Python) / `xs.zip(ys).forEach` → Motoi: **`for-each`** with two lists (R7RS-small supports multi-list `for-each`)

```scheme
;; zip + forEach -> multi-list for-each. R7RS-small for-each is already multi-list.
(let ((sums '()))
  (for-each (lambda (x y) (set! sums (cons (+ x y) sums)))
            (list 1 2 3)
            (list 10 20 30))
  (reverse sums))
```

## Where there is no analog

Some other-dialect verbs point at concepts Motoi does not carry, and the honest entry is a null:

- other-dialect `import numpy` / typed n-d arrays → Motoi: **honest null.** No array library; use lists and vectors with ordinary arithmetic.
- other-dialect raw pointers / manual `malloc` → Motoi: **honest null.** No pointer model.
- other-dialect buffers / `interactive` editor commands → Motoi: **honest null.** Not an editor's language.
- other-dialect ownership / borrow-checking → Motoi: **honest null.** No ownership model.
- other-dialect goroutines / channels → Motoi: **honest null.** No concurrency primitives.
- other-dialect regex matching → Motoi: **honest null** for pattern matching; `string-contains` for literal substring search.
- other-dialect class definitions / `class Foo(Bar)` → Motoi: **honest null** for inheritance; use closures or hash tables to model objects.
- other-dialect generics / type parameters → Motoi: **honest null.** No static type system.

For the array case specifically, the redirect is real even though the library isn't: numeric work over a list of numbers is plain arithmetic mapped across the list, and it runs:

```scheme
;; No array library, but numeric list work is real: mean of a list.
(let* ((xs (list 2 4 6 8 10))
       (n (length xs))
       (total (fold + 0 xs)))
  (exact->inexact (/ total n)))
```

## Using the table

Scan for the operation you want by its familiar name in the left column of your memory, then reach for the Motoi verb in the fence. Every Motoi side here is verified to run, so you can lift it straight into your own code. The shape of the table is the shape of the whole book: the *idea* almost always crosses the boundary intact — mapping is mapping, folding is folding, looking up is looking up — and only the spelling changes. When even the idea doesn't cross, the honest null is the true and complete answer, and the redirect points you at the nearest thing Motoi really has.")
